WEBVTT

00:00:11.010 --> 00:00:15.540
My right hand holds a bowl of gold,

00:00:15.540 --> 00:00:20.080
And my left holds one of silver.

00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:24.620
Never one without the other,

00:00:24.620 --> 00:00:37.700
Two unseen bowls for each of us.

00:00:37.700 --> 00:00:46.110
The golden one is filled with joy,

00:00:46.110 --> 00:00:53.450
shining warmly.

00:00:53.450 --> 00:00:58.250
Since we met, my golden bowl

00:00:58.250 --> 00:01:05.260
cannot hold all my happiness and love.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:15.400
Golden joy, silver sadness,

00:01:15.400 --> 00:01:22.750
I would leave my past behind...

00:01:22.750 --> 00:01:27.480
For you, for the sake of love,

00:01:27.480 --> 00:01:34.420
I would empty the bowls of my past.

00:01:58.310 --> 00:02:04.390
[...then Lebrand picked up the scythe, and cleared with it a circular space,]

00:02:04.390 --> 00:02:08.590
[...three or four yards in diameter, just below the insect.]

00:02:08.860 --> 00:02:13.800
[Then he told Jupiter to let the string go, and come down from the tree.]

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:17.530
That's good. Next, Miss Misonoo.

00:02:18.130 --> 00:02:19.340
Yes...

00:02:20.870 --> 00:02:23.870
[Lebrand placed a small stick into the ground]

00:02:23.870 --> 00:02:27.140
[...at the exact place where the insect was buried.]

00:02:27.140 --> 00:02:33.480
[He took from his pocket a long tape measure. He fastened it down and...]

00:02:33.680 --> 00:02:36.750
Resign, of your own volition.

00:02:36.750 --> 00:02:39.820
We can't tolerate such an injustice!

00:02:44.900 --> 00:02:50.300
[...he went in front of his master, clearing away the bushes with a spade.] <b> </b>

00:02:50.300 --> 00:02:50.630
[...he went in front of his master, clearing away the bushes with a spade.] Ok, that will do.

00:02:50.630 --> 00:02:51.840
Ok, that will do.

00:02:52.440 --> 00:02:54.710
What's wrong? You seem unwell!

00:02:56.170 --> 00:02:56.970
Yes, well... <b> </b>

00:02:56.970 --> 00:02:59.310
Yes, well... Next, Miss Yoshimoto...

00:02:59.310 --> 00:03:00.310
Yes!

00:03:00.710 --> 00:03:04.920
[At the distance of fifty feet, Lebrand stopped,]

00:03:05.520 --> 00:03:08.790
[...and put the second stick into the ground.]

00:03:09.390 --> 00:03:14.060
[The ground around it was again cleared in a large circle, about four feet deep...] <b> </b> <b> </b>

00:03:14.060 --> 00:03:17.460
[The ground around it was again cleared in a large circle, about four feet deep...] "The unqualified person should leave the Sorority.."

00:03:18.400 --> 00:03:20.800
Such poor losers.

00:03:26.140 --> 00:03:27.600
Don't let it bother you.

00:03:28.470 --> 00:03:29.540
Ok...

00:03:33.340 --> 00:03:34.540
Stand!

00:03:37.680 --> 00:03:41.950
I found a nice Kyoto-style coffee shop at the train station!

00:03:42.490 --> 00:03:43.620
I'm going home. <b> </b>

00:03:43.620 --> 00:03:47.220
I'm going home. Come on, let's go!

00:03:47.220 --> 00:03:48.760
No, go ahead without me.

00:03:49.160 --> 00:03:53.030
It's really good - their shiratama is wonderful...!

00:03:54.570 --> 00:03:56.700
I need to throw these in the incinerator.

00:03:57.230 --> 00:03:58.500
What's that?

00:04:00.500 --> 00:04:02.910
I found them in my desk this morning...

00:04:17.250 --> 00:04:23.060
7. The Darkness in the Clock Tower

00:04:34.740 --> 00:04:36.010
Brother...

00:04:36.540 --> 00:04:38.740
I don't understand what's wrong.

00:04:39.410 --> 00:04:41.810
I don't understand what's so hateful about me.

00:04:43.280 --> 00:04:46.020
I wanted to be liked by everyone.

00:04:46.950 --> 00:04:54.830
I wanted to be liked just a little - enough not to be hurt, or to hurt someone.

00:04:55.430 --> 00:04:58.030
That was enough and is still enough for me.

00:04:58.500 --> 00:05:01.630
Then, why am I hated so much...

00:05:01.630 --> 00:05:05.240
...by so many?

00:05:06.040 --> 00:05:09.640
What did I do?

00:05:10.040 --> 00:05:13.380
What have I done to deserve this?

00:05:14.650 --> 00:05:19.920
What is... What on earth is wrong with me?

00:05:20.320 --> 00:05:22.850
I can't... I can't stand it!

00:05:36.600 --> 00:05:38.400
So... this is the clock tower?

00:05:59.760 --> 00:06:04.230
"M-sama, thinking of you has turned me into ashes."

00:06:07.830 --> 00:06:11.840
"Say you love me once again. That will restore the life in me."

00:06:16.570 --> 00:06:18.040
"I want you."

00:06:23.380 --> 00:06:25.580
I'm not alone.

00:06:27.450 --> 00:06:34.390
There have been many before me who came here to cry.

00:06:37.800 --> 00:06:43.940
When they lost their courage to continue, they would come to this dark tower.

00:06:44.670 --> 00:06:49.140
When they lost love, and when they lost friendship...

00:06:49.540 --> 00:06:53.810
They found, in this tower, a place to escape -

00:06:55.280 --> 00:06:58.950
...to embrace themselves and wet their knees with their warm tears...

00:06:59.620 --> 00:07:07.360
Last year, the year before last, and many many years before that...

00:07:07.690 --> 00:07:12.560
So many sisters over these many years, coming here to share their pain...

00:07:21.510 --> 00:07:23.040
What was that sound?

00:07:54.340 --> 00:07:55.610
Saint-Juste-sama...

00:08:01.210 --> 00:08:04.020
Smoking... she's smoking?

00:08:05.620 --> 00:08:08.090
She... she is bad!

00:08:10.760 --> 00:08:11.820
Excuse me...?

00:08:29.980 --> 00:08:31.510
Pick them up, won't you...

00:08:31.780 --> 00:08:32.580
What?

00:08:37.980 --> 00:08:39.190
Oh! Ok.

00:08:42.060 --> 00:08:42.990
I see...

00:08:43.320 --> 00:08:46.930
This must have been the sound I heard earlier...

00:08:47.990 --> 00:08:50.730
There are so many marks here.

00:08:51.600 --> 00:08:53.000
She's done this before.

00:08:54.730 --> 00:08:55.800
What's this...?

00:08:56.000 --> 00:08:57.340
...this silhouette!

00:08:58.470 --> 00:09:01.810
It's Miya-sama! It's a silhouette of Miya-sama!

00:09:13.220 --> 00:09:14.150
Thanks.

00:10:07.340 --> 00:10:08.410
Ummm...

00:10:08.740 --> 00:10:10.340
Is that Miya-sama?

00:10:13.350 --> 00:10:14.080
Yes.

00:10:14.480 --> 00:10:15.620
But why?

00:10:16.150 --> 00:10:19.220
They are so deep and so... many.

00:10:20.820 --> 00:10:23.220
Like the rains which fall in this world...

00:10:23.760 --> 00:10:24.630
What?

00:10:26.630 --> 00:10:29.230
...the tears also fall in my heart.

00:10:30.160 --> 00:10:35.170
What is it for, the sadness which creeps into my heart...

00:10:44.780 --> 00:10:47.180
What is this sadness for?

00:10:56.460 --> 00:10:58.990
What is this sadness for?

00:11:09.000 --> 00:11:10.000
Saint-Juste...

00:11:11.070 --> 00:11:12.070
Saint-Juste...

00:11:12.740 --> 00:11:16.010
The name has an echo of loneliness in it...

00:11:16.740 --> 00:11:18.680
And about Saint-Juste-sama and Miya-sama...

00:11:19.280 --> 00:11:23.680
...there is a mystery between them I cannot understand.

00:11:25.890 --> 00:11:28.020
Like the rain...

00:11:28.490 --> 00:11:30.960
...the tears fall in my heart.

00:11:31.960 --> 00:11:33.160
Saint-Juste...

00:11:33.560 --> 00:11:36.630
Who named her Saint-Juste?

00:11:37.570 --> 00:11:40.840
Who on earth... is Saint Juste?

00:11:53.980 --> 00:11:56.850
I only have twelve minutes to catch that train, or I'll be late!

00:12:11.000 --> 00:12:12.800
Twelve Minutes!!! Finally!

00:12:26.410 --> 00:12:29.680
She won't be able to go home together with you from now on.

00:12:29.880 --> 00:12:33.820
As a member of the Sorority, she has a lot of socializing to do.

00:12:34.020 --> 00:12:36.630
She asked me to tell you this.

00:12:36.760 --> 00:12:41.430
I want to hear from her directly! Where is she?!

00:12:41.430 --> 00:12:44.500
Being her friend, can't you understand why...

00:12:44.500 --> 00:12:45.630
What do you mean by that!

00:12:46.840 --> 00:12:50.570
That's why she asked me to tell you.

00:12:54.640 --> 00:12:58.450
I'd not be so easily hurt if she told me herself!

00:13:17.200 --> 00:13:18.400
Good Morning.

00:13:23.670 --> 00:13:24.810
Good Morning.

00:13:25.140 --> 00:13:27.810
Can I... call you some time?

00:13:28.810 --> 00:13:29.810
Maybe...?

00:14:01.640 --> 00:14:02.910
Oh, Misonoo-san!

00:14:03.780 --> 00:14:06.520
Let's go shopping for material for the pajamas we're sewing!

00:14:07.050 --> 00:14:08.920
Oh, for home economics class...

00:14:09.120 --> 00:14:12.050
It's early next week. So let's go today?

00:14:12.320 --> 00:14:14.860
Oh! Well... I don't think...

00:14:15.930 --> 00:14:17.330
You're busy with something else?

00:14:17.660 --> 00:14:20.000
Yes, sort of...

00:14:20.000 --> 00:14:21.060
The library!

00:14:21.200 --> 00:14:22.730
I have to find a book there...

00:14:22.870 --> 00:14:25.470
If I don't go today, I'd have to go next week.

00:14:25.800 --> 00:14:26.800
So you see...

00:14:26.800 --> 00:14:28.340
You hard worker, you!

00:14:28.540 --> 00:14:30.070
No, no, that's not it...

00:14:30.070 --> 00:14:33.010
I get it! You're in a jam.

00:14:33.340 --> 00:14:35.410
In that case, I'll choose your pattern too.

00:14:36.080 --> 00:14:37.010
What?

00:14:37.480 --> 00:14:40.550
That way you can go to the library!

00:15:15.190 --> 00:15:17.990
Can I borrow your light?

00:15:18.660 --> 00:15:22.330
If you're caught, you'll be suspended from school... or expelled!

00:15:23.660 --> 00:15:26.060
I adore expulsion.

00:15:29.200 --> 00:15:30.670
I'll take those.

00:15:30.930 --> 00:15:32.340
And I adore...

00:15:32.940 --> 00:15:34.070
Here!

00:15:41.750 --> 00:15:43.680
Does your wound still hurt?

00:15:45.280 --> 00:15:46.420
No..

00:15:47.750 --> 00:15:48.820
Good.

00:16:11.640 --> 00:16:14.650
Let's see... ummm...

00:16:15.580 --> 00:16:17.310
Where shall I start?

00:16:18.520 --> 00:16:20.250
You'll find it on the shelf over there. <b> </b>

00:16:20.250 --> 00:16:22.190
You'll find it on the shelf over there. Oh! Thanks...

00:16:22.190 --> 00:16:25.320
Wait! The shelf over there??? What?

00:16:25.520 --> 00:16:29.930
You want to learn about The French Revolution and Saint-Juste.

00:16:30.730 --> 00:16:33.600
Yes! But... but how...

00:16:34.130 --> 00:16:36.870
The freshmen will all be in front of these books.

00:16:36.870 --> 00:16:41.540
on the French Revolution and Saint-Juste in three months.

00:16:42.010 --> 00:16:44.270
Well... I didn't mean that...

00:16:45.210 --> 00:16:46.340
Hey, no problem!

00:16:46.480 --> 00:16:50.210
Reading for any reason is always better then not reading at all.

00:16:51.220 --> 00:16:52.620
I'll show you where they are.

00:16:53.280 --> 00:16:54.020
Sorry for the trouble...

00:16:55.020 --> 00:16:58.220
Let's see, there's this, and this...

00:16:58.690 --> 00:16:59.820
And finally, this.

00:17:00.420 --> 00:17:01.360
Thanks...

00:17:02.490 --> 00:17:03.890
So funny!

00:17:03.960 --> 00:17:07.430
But then I saw Ide-san and Kooriyama-san at the Paris Hotel...

00:17:07.430 --> 00:17:08.770
No way! <b> </b>

00:17:08.770 --> 00:17:10.100
No way! Wow!!!!

00:17:11.300 --> 00:17:13.440
And then? What then?

00:17:13.440 --> 00:17:15.310
Well, you know Urayama-san...

00:17:16.440 --> 00:17:19.510
Hey, where do you think you are?

00:17:19.510 --> 00:17:22.510
This is a library. If you want to talk, go outside.

00:17:23.510 --> 00:17:24.380
Ok.

00:17:24.580 --> 00:17:27.180
Excuse me, I'd like to borrow these.

00:17:33.060 --> 00:17:36.460
One can't even read peacefully in the library these days!

00:17:36.990 --> 00:17:39.660
You like books so much, Kaoru-sama?

00:17:39.860 --> 00:17:40.800
Surprised?

00:17:41.870 --> 00:17:43.800
Well... a bit.

00:17:44.740 --> 00:17:46.400
I've heard that from someone else...

00:17:49.140 --> 00:17:50.480
Saint-Juste-sama!

00:17:50.810 --> 00:17:51.940
Yes.

00:17:56.810 --> 00:17:59.420
Rei was transferred into our school in junior high school.

00:18:00.080 --> 00:18:01.820
She was really different.

00:18:05.890 --> 00:18:08.630
She seemed to always be alone, reading books...

00:18:08.960 --> 00:18:11.630
...showing no interest in her surroundings.

00:18:18.500 --> 00:18:19.640
Watch out!

00:18:35.250 --> 00:18:36.320
Cool!

00:18:37.520 --> 00:18:38.790
What are you reading?

00:18:39.460 --> 00:18:42.330
I'm sure it wouldn't interest you... being such an athlete...

00:18:45.130 --> 00:18:47.070
Oh, it's Verlaine.

00:18:47.270 --> 00:18:48.200
What?

00:18:48.670 --> 00:18:50.740
"As rain falls..."

00:18:51.400 --> 00:18:52.540
Right?

00:18:54.140 --> 00:18:55.470
Not bad!

00:18:56.070 --> 00:18:57.140
Pretty cool!

00:18:57.810 --> 00:18:59.880
Now we're even.

00:19:02.750 --> 00:19:05.620
Then I recruited Rei for our basketball team.

00:19:06.080 --> 00:19:07.550
She played basketball!?

00:19:08.690 --> 00:19:10.690
She easily became a star player.

00:19:13.430 --> 00:19:16.700
She had such life in her when she was playing basketball...

00:19:17.630 --> 00:19:19.230
...and her eyes glowed.

00:19:20.170 --> 00:19:22.430
That's why I liked watching her...

00:19:23.570 --> 00:19:25.040
...or so I told myself.

00:19:28.240 --> 00:19:30.380
But that wasn't it.

00:19:34.580 --> 00:19:36.180
But, what really attracted me to her was...

00:19:36.520 --> 00:19:38.980
...was something inhuman in her nature;

00:19:40.190 --> 00:19:43.390
and those eyes with such a distant, far-away look...

00:19:44.460 --> 00:19:45.720
Far away...?

00:19:46.330 --> 00:19:50.860
What does she see so far away? What lies deep within her soul?

00:19:50.860 --> 00:19:51.860
What could it be?

00:20:08.210 --> 00:20:09.880
That smells good!

00:20:10.280 --> 00:20:12.750
Cookies are baking!

00:20:14.620 --> 00:20:17.690
Oh yes... it must be from Tomoko's cooking club...

00:20:32.710 --> 00:20:34.110
You're really something!

00:20:34.910 --> 00:20:38.980
Making overtures not only to Miya-sama, but now to Kaoru-no-Kimi as well.

00:20:39.780 --> 00:20:42.520
You took after your mother the "hostess"...

00:20:42.920 --> 00:20:44.850
...who will... with anyone, right?

00:20:46.190 --> 00:20:47.990
So what do you want?

00:20:48.190 --> 00:20:51.260
Here. You left it at school.

00:20:51.590 --> 00:20:52.790
What?

00:20:53.460 --> 00:20:55.930
It was in the incinerator!

00:21:07.670 --> 00:21:10.540
Look at that... Miss Sorority has fallen!

00:21:12.810 --> 00:21:14.410
Nanako!

00:21:14.410 --> 00:21:16.880
Are you all right? Nanako! Nanako!!

00:21:17.680 --> 00:21:19.950
You!! What did you do to Nanako?

00:21:20.350 --> 00:21:23.360
Wh... what? We didn't do anything!

00:21:23.360 --> 00:21:25.630
That's right! She just fell down by herself!

00:21:26.960 --> 00:21:30.830
If you mess with Nanako, you'll be facing me for it!

00:21:30.830 --> 00:21:33.430
If you ever treat her mean you'll be dealing with me. Got that?

00:21:34.970 --> 00:21:36.100
Tomoko...

00:21:46.050 --> 00:21:46.910
Tomoko?

00:21:49.980 --> 00:21:51.320
Hey...

00:21:52.320 --> 00:21:53.390
It's ok...

00:21:53.790 --> 00:21:54.920
...to call me.

00:21:59.130 --> 00:22:00.060
Tomoko....

00:22:08.140 --> 00:22:09.470
On second thought, I'll call you.

00:22:09.740 --> 00:22:10.740
Just like always.

00:22:19.280 --> 00:22:21.950
Leon de Saint-Juste was a young knight.

00:22:22.550 --> 00:22:27.350
At eighteen, his heart broken by love, he was a dissolute young Parisian.

00:22:27.350 --> 00:22:30.560
He attended Darcy University and studied Law.

00:22:33.760 --> 00:22:38.030
After the French Revolution he joined with Robespierre of the Jacobin Club

00:22:38.030 --> 00:22:42.040
And he sent many of the nobility and royalty to the guillotine.

00:22:42.040 --> 00:22:47.840
His feminine beauty and cruelty made him both feared and hated,

00:22:47.840 --> 00:22:51.180
And he became known as the "Angel of Death."

00:22:55.980 --> 00:22:59.520
In 1794 his party lost power,

00:23:02.920 --> 00:23:08.530
...and at age 24, he was guillotined alongside his friend, Robespierre.

00:23:11.470 --> 00:23:15.670
Like the rains which fall in this world, tears also fall in my heart.

00:23:16.000 --> 00:23:20.270
What is it creeping into my heart, filling it with sadness...

00:23:22.610 --> 00:23:24.150
Angel of Death...

00:23:25.550 --> 00:23:32.420
This was Saint-Juste of the French Revolution: he gazed into death - even his own - with cool detachment.

00:23:34.090 --> 00:23:39.490
Does her nickname reveal the sad vision which is reflected in her eyes?

00:23:40.490 --> 00:23:44.030
Could it be a vision of Death?

00:23:47.300 --> 00:23:48.570
My brother...

00:24:09.990 --> 00:24:14.200
I dreamed I was chasing a rainbow...

00:24:14.200 --> 00:24:19.670
Then the rainbow I was chasing was you.

00:24:21.140 --> 00:24:25.270
Before, I had no strength, no will.

00:24:25.270 --> 00:24:30.750
But now because of you, I do.

00:24:31.480 --> 00:24:37.020
Feelings of love, like raindrops

00:24:37.020 --> 00:24:42.490
Come pouring from the sky.

00:24:42.490 --> 00:24:45.230
This is surely a game

00:24:45.230 --> 00:24:48.030
Of some mischievous fairy...

00:24:48.030 --> 00:24:50.430
Always dancing,

00:24:50.430 --> 00:24:55.700
Always capricious...

00:25:03.450 --> 00:25:06.520
Mariko gives an extravagant birthday party...

00:25:06.780 --> 00:25:10.590
But... Nanako is the only guest!

00:25:11.320 --> 00:25:15.190
After the party, Mariko invites Nanako to her home.

00:25:15.790 --> 00:25:19.130
But Nanako is in for much more than she bargained for...

00:25:19.660 --> 00:25:20.800
Next episode: <b> </b>

00:25:20.800 --> 00:25:22.670
Next episode: I Want You...

00:25:22.860 --> 00:25:24.470
Brother, Dear Brother... <b> </b>

00:25:24.470 --> 00:25:27.870
Brother, Dear Brother... There is no end to my tears...
